st selected mood: {{MOOD}}.":"","A short grounding pause or a slower moment may help. Open Quick tools if you want to try one.":"","Could you message someone you trust and let them know you would like company? The support page has more options.":"","If possible, take one small break: sit somewhere comfortable, get some water, or step away briefly.":"","Write down just one next step. The small-step planner in Quick tools can help you keep it manageable.":"","If you may be in immediate danger, call your local emergency number now. In India, call 112. Move near someone you trust if you can.":"","I’m really sorry things feel this hard. I’m not able to keep you safe through a chat. If you or someone else may be in immediate danger, call your local emergency number now and go to someone you trust who can stay with you. In India, call 112 for emergencies or 14416 for Tele-MANAS support. If you’re elsewhere, find local support at findahelpline.com.":"","Mind Care — a student-made wellbeing space":"","Mind Care is a student-made wellbeing dashboard for everyone, with a private mood check-in, supportive AI chat, calming tools, and helpline information.":"","Skip to content":"","Mind Care home":"","mind care":"",".":"","Main navigation":"","Home":"","Topics":"","Get the app":"","Need help?":"","Take a moment":"","A student-made wellbeing space":"","A little pause":"","for":"","real life.":"","Stress can come from school, work, relationships, or just having a lot on your mind. Check in, try a small reset, and find support—at your own pace.":"","Explore the topics":"","Find a quick reset":"","A student project, made to be useful to everyone.":"","A simple illustration of a person resting":"","✿":"","Take it one day at a time.":"","YOUR WELLBEING TOOLKIT":"","SCROLL TO BEGIN ↓":"","01 / Pick what feels useful":"","A few ways":"","to":"","begin.":"","Choose a topic to open its own page. There’s no set order, and you can come back here whenever you like.":"","AI chat":"","Talk something through":"","Mood check-in":"","Notice how you feel":"","Focus timer":"","Study with gentle break reminders":"","Daily care":"","Choose a few kind steps for today":"","What do I need?":"","Find a gentle next step":"","Private journal":"","Write a note for yourself":"","Quick tools":"","Breathing and grounding":"","Sleep tips":"","Build a softer wind-down":"","Helplines & support":"","Find someone to talk to":"","About this project":"","Why a student made this":"","Android app":"","Get Mind Care for your phone":"","Use just one topic or explore them all at your own pace.":"","Mind Care, in your pocket":"","A little care,":"","wherever you are.":"","Take the student-made wellbeing tools with you. The Android app is designed to keep your journal and check-ins on your device.":"","Mind Care for Android":"","Android APK · debug build":"","Download APK":"","Check again":"","Only install APK files you trust. Android may ask you to allow installation from your browser. The app’s AI chat needs an internet connection; saved wellbeing entries stay on this device.":"","A gentle chat, if you need one":"","Put it into":"","words.":"","Share what’s on your mind and get a supportive response or a small idea to try. You can also use the quick prompts.":"","A note before you start":"","Mind Care is an AI, not a therapist. Google Gemini processes messages to create replies. This site doesn’t save the conversation, but":"","Google’s AI terms":"","apply. Avoid sharing names, addresses, or anything very private.":"","Mind Care chat":"","Here to listen":"","AI · NOT A THERAPIST":"","Hi. What’s on your mind today? Share as much or as little as you like.":"","Suggested messages":"","I feel stressed":"","Help me clear my head":"","I can’t sleep":"","Write a message":"","Write what’s on your mind…":"","Send message":"","↑":"","A gentle study companion":"","Make room":"","focus.":"","Pick a short focus block or a small break. You can pause or stop whenever you need to.":"","This timer runs on this device and does not send anything online.":"","CHOOSE A SESSION":"","Choose timer session":"","Focus · 25 min":"","Short break · 5 min":"","25 minutes remaining":"","25:00":"","Start focus":"","Small things count":"","A little care":"","today.":"","Choose any small steps that feel kind and realistic. This is not a streak or a score—skipping a day is okay.":"","Your choices are saved only in this browser on this device and reset each day.":"","MY GENTLE CHECKLIST":"","Drink a glass of water":"","Take a short stretch or outside pause":"","Reach out to someone I trust":"","0/3 small care steps marked today.":"","A quiet place for your thoughts":"","Write it out,":"","just for you.":"","You don’t need to make it sound a certain way. A few words about what’s on your mind is enough.":"","Saved only on this device":"","Your note stays in this browser and isn’t sent to a server. If this is a shared device, someone else using this browser may be able to read it.":"","What would you like to write?":"","Start anywhere. What happened today? What do you need right now?":"","Save on this device":"","Delete my note":"","01 / A little check-in":"","How are you":"","feeling":"","today?":"","There’s no right answer. You might be stressed about work, school, relationships, family, or something you can’t quite put into words.":"","RIGHT NOW, I FEEL…":"","Choose how you feel":"","Overwhelmed":"","Anxious":"","A little low":"","Doing okay":"","Your current selection stays on this page. Mood history is saved only in this browser.":"","Your mood history":"","Clear history":"","Your last seven days":"","Check-ins you choose to save will appear here. This is for reflection, not diagnosis.":"","02 / Quick tools":"","Find a reset":"","that":"","fits.":"","Pick one thing that feels doable. Skip anything that doesn’t feel right for you.":"","01":"","Take a slower breath":"","Give yourself a short pause. Follow the circle if that feels comfortable.":"","Breathe normally if focusing on your breath feels uncomfortable.":"","02":"","Come back to now":"","Notice what’s around you, one sense at a time. Take your time with each step.":"","things you can see":"","things you can feel":"","things you can hear":"","things you can smell":"","thing you can taste":"","Take your time. You can skip any step.":"","03":"","Untangle one task":"","Write down what’s on your mind. Choose a tiny next step, not the whole solution.":"","One thing on my mind":"","e.g. send that email":"","Make it smaller":"","My small-step planner":"","Optional date":"","Add to my plan":"","Your plan stays in this browser on this device.":"","04":"","A gentle body pause":"","Let your shoulders soften if that feels okay. Notice where your body is supported, without needing to change anything.":"","Try this pause":"","You can stop or skip this whenever you want.":"","05":"","Listen for a moment":"","Notice one sound nearby, then one farther away. No need to label it as good or bad.":"","Take a listening pause":"","Stay with this moment for as long as feels useful.":"","A small check-in with yourself":"","What might help":"","right now?":"","Choose what feels closest. This is only a starting point—you know yourself best.":"","Choose what you need":"","A little calm":"","Someone to talk to":"","Rest or a break":"","Help with one next step":"","I may be unsafe right now":"","03 / A gentler wind-down":"","Give your day":"","a softer":"","ending.":"","Sleep can be affected by lots of things. You don’t need a perfect routine—try one small change that feels realistic.":"","Build my wind-down":"","Ideas for winding down":"","Make tomorrow a little easier":"","Write down one thing you need to remember, then leave it for tomorrow.":"","Dim the day":"","Lower the lights or put your screen away for a few minutes if you can.":"","Let your body slow down":"","Try a comfortable stretch, quiet music, or a few unhurried breaths.":"","Keep it kind and flexible":"","If sleep feels difficult, resting quietly still counts as a pause.":"","04 / Getting support":"","It’s okay to":"","reach out.":"","Need urgent help?":"","If you or someone else is in immediate danger, call your local emergency number now. In India, call":"","If you’re struggling, talking with someone you trust or a qualified professional may help. You deserve care, whatever you’re going through.":"","A":"","Talk to someone you trust":"","A friend, family member, colleague, teacher, counselor, or healthcare professional.":"","B":"","In India: Tele-MANAS":"","for free mental health support.":"","Official service":"",". For other countries, find local options at":"","findahelpline.com":"","C":"","Immediate danger?":"","Call your local emergency number. In India, call":"","This student-made project is for everyone and shares general wellbeing ideas, not medical advice or a crisis service. If you feel unsafe, contact emergency help now.":"","Your trusted contacts":"","Add people or local services you have checked yourself. These entries are stored only in this browser and are not verified emergency services.":"","Contact name":"","Phone number or link":"","Save contact":"","A note from the creator":"","Why we made":"","this.":"","Developers:":"","Class / course:":"","We made Mind Care as a student project because looking after your wellbeing can feel confusing, and starting a conversation isn’t always easy. We wanted to make one friendly page with a few simple ways to pause and find help. It’s for everyone, whatever life looks like for you.":"","A quick privacy note:":"","Mood history, plans, daily care choices, contacts, feedback, and journal notes are saved only in this browser on this device and may be visible to others who use it. Chat messages are sent to Google Gemini for a reply. In the online language build, fixed interface text (not personal entries) is sent to the configured translation service when you choose a new language. Check translations against official sources before relying on support information. See":"",". This is a student project, not professional or emergency care.":"","Display settings":"","Larger text":"","Higher contrast":"","Languages, online and offline":"","A complete build can include English, Hinglish, and all 22 scheduled Indian languages. The website caches every included language on the first online visit; the Android app can include them in its installation. AI chat needs an internet connection.":"","Share feedback":"","Leave a suggestion for this project. Feedback is saved only in this browser on this device.":"","Your suggestion":"","What could make this site more useful?":"","Save feedback here":"","Check that the helpline information is right for your audience before sharing the project.":"","You made it here. That counts.":"","Back to top":"","Back to the beginning ↑":"","A student-made project to remind everyone that they matter.":"","For anyone, made with care":""}}
